## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates practical data-structure composition: a queue with constant-time min tracking, a common interview pattern for streams and real-time dashboards.

## Key Concepts

- Two-stack queue pattern
- Per-stack min tracking
- Amortized analysis and edge-case handling for duplicates

## Code Example

```javascript
class MinQueue {
  constructor(){ this.inStack = []; this.outStack = []; }
  enqueue(x){ const minIn = this.inStack.length ? Math.min(x, this.inStack[this.inStack.length-1][1]) : x; this.inStack.push([x, minIn]); }
  dequeue(){ if (!this.outStack.length){ while (this.inStack.length){ const [val] = this.inStack.pop(); const minOut = this.outStack.length ? Math.min(val, this.outStack[this.outStack.length-1][1]) : val; this.outStack.push([val, minOut]); } }
    const popped = this.outStack.pop(); return popped ? popped[0] : undefined; }
  getMin(){ const minIn = this.inStack.length ? this.inStack[this.inStack.length-1][1] : Infinity; const minOut = this.outStack.length ? this.outStack[this.outStack.length-1][1] : Infinity; return Math.min(minIn, minOut); }
}
```

